work-order.text:
{
  "acceptance": [
    {
      "check": "Signed-in user creates a group (name, currency, type) and sees it in the home group list with its per-group balance slot; opening a group they do not belong to (or that does not exist) returns an indistinguishable 404 with no data leak, and signed-out access redirects to sign-in.",
      "id": "AC-1"
    },
    {
      "check": "Missing-or-forbidden group reads are indistinguishable at the data layer: the membership guard returns 404 whether the group is absent, the caller is a non-member, or the id is malformed, and unit tests assert all paths carry no group fields.",
      "id": "AC-2"
    },
    {
      "check": "Owner copies an invite link; signed-in non-member B opens /join/<token> and claims placeholder 'Bo' as the join itself (the claim adopts the placeholder row, no separate member row first); owner rotates (old link dead) then disables (join rejected), each behind an explicit confirm naming the link; double-claim of 'Bo' is rejected.",
      "id": "AC-3"
    },
    {
      "check": "Remove-member, archive and leave flows each require an explicit confirm naming the object and succeed for zero-balance members; rename applies directly with a success note and no confirm step.",
      "id": "AC-4"
    },
    {
      "check": "Every group read and write is authorized on the server against the session user via the (sessionUser, groupScope, zod-validated input) pattern: unauthenticated calls get 401/redirect, non-members get 404, invalid input gets a user-safe validation error; negative matrix covered by tests.",
      "id": "AC-5"
    },
    {
      "check": "New screens (home list, group detail header + settings shell, members-and-invite) use only ui.md tokens, keep one h1 with hierarchical headings, labelled controls with visible focus, and designed empty/loading/error states.",
      "id": "AC-6"
    },
    {
      "check": "Removal or leave with a non-zero balance is blocked with a message pointing at settle-up, and removal/leave paths call the zero-balance guard seam.",
      "id": "AC-7"
    },
    {
      "check": "Every membership change (join, claim-as-join, leave, remove) writes an ActivityEvent row with actor and timestamp in the same transaction as the change.",
      "id": "AC-8"
    },
    {
      "check": "A stale second claim of an already-claimed placeholder seat shows the 'That seat has already been claimed.' rejection on the join page instead of silently refreshing; the seat stays with the first claimant and the loser is still offered a plain join.",
      "id": "AC-9"
    },
    {
      "check": "Renaming a group applies on save with a 'Renamed to …' note and no confirm step; remove, archive, leave, rotate and disable keep their naming confirms.",
      "id": "AC-10"
    }
  ],
  "approach": "Amend the criterion where the criterion was wrong, and change the mechanism where the code was wrong — two different fixes, not one patch. AC-4 is corrected to what docs/ui.md already says: remove/archive/leave (plus rotate/disable) keep their naming confirms, while rename keeps its direct save plus success note (T-5's flow); no rename component is touched. The silent double-claim is fixed by moving failure feedback out of the component the action's own revalidation unmounts: claimPlaceholder stops returning inline error state for the two shapes a stale join page can actually produce and redirects instead — seat-taken goes to /join/<token>?claim=taken, rendered as a panel-level alert above the (now empty) seat list with the plain join still offered, and already-a-member goes to the group page, consistent with the page-load member bounce. Malformed-input and invalid-token errors stay inline because they never re-render the list. Unit tests assert the redirects; the atomic UPDATE … WHERE user_id IS NULL plus 23505 coverage is untouched.",
  "confidence": 82,
  "confidence_rationale": "BUG-2 resolves by evidence rather than judgment: ui.md destructive-actions list, T-5's passing flow, and the implementation all agree rename has no confirm, so amending AC-4 cannot break a passing test. BUG-1's mechanism is confirmed in code and matches QA's observed empty-seat silent refresh; redirect-with-message is the standard Next pattern for exactly this unmount hazard and is unit-assertable. Held below 90 because no live preview was available and the already-member-to-group-page redirect is a small behavior change beyond the reported bug.",
  "evidence": [
    "docs/ui.md destructive-actions list gates only delete-expense, delete-payment, remove-member, rotate/disable-invite and archive-group behind confirms — rename absent",
    "preflight clean on work-order.json version 2 (node .sdlc/bin/preflight.mjs --issue 5)",
    "No failure-packet.json, previous-output.json, or stop.json present — plain QA-fail root-cause revision, no mechanical-failure or refusal path"
  ],
  "files": [
    {
      "action": "edit",
      "change": "claimPlaceholder: the seat-taken outcome redirects to /join/<token>?claim=taken and the already-member outcome redirects to the group page instead of returning inline error state that the revalidation unmounts; malformed-input and invalid-token errors stay inline.",
      "path": "lib/groups/actions.ts"
    },
    {
      "action": "edit",
      "change": "Read the claim=taken search param and pass it to JoinPanel as a notice prop; the signed-out redirect, member bounce to the group page, and invalid-token 404 are unchanged.",
      "path": "app/join/[token]/page.tsx"
    },
    {
      "action": "edit",
      "change": "JoinPanel renders a panel-level alert (role=alert, aria-live polite) for the claim notice above the seat list with the plain join still offered; ClaimSeatForm keeps inline StateMessage for validation errors only.",
      "path": "components/groups-panels.tsx"
    },
    {
      "action": "edit",
      "change": "Export a shared CLAIM_TAKEN query constant ('taken') used by the claim redirect and the join page, so the two sides cannot drift.",
      "path": "lib/groups/validation.ts"
    }
  ],
  "issue": 5,
  "kind": "feature",
  "mode": "committed",
  "qa_script": [
    "Sign up as A, create group 'Goa trip' (INR, trip), assert it lists with a balance slot.",
    "As A: Members screen shows owner badge; add placeholder 'Bo' by name; copy invite link.",
    "Open the link signed-out and assert redirect to sign-in (not a 404); sign in as B with the token preserved, claim 'Bo' as the join; assert member list shows B and the placeholder gone.",
    "Two-browser race: B and C load the join page, B claims 'Bo' and joins; C clicks the stale claim button and assert C sees the 'That seat has already been claimed.' rejection on /join with a plain join still offered, never becoming a member.",
    "As A rotate the link with the confirm naming the link; open the old link as C and assert expired; disable the link and assert join is rejected.",
    "Rename applies on Save name with a 'Renamed to …' note and no confirm; remove, archive and leave-as-sole-member each show a confirm naming the object (zero-balance flows only; the non-zero block is unit-proven)."
  ],
  "reproduced": false,
  "risks": [
    "T-10 as currently written asserts the old AC-4 letter (a rename confirm); the next QA run must be re-derived from the amended AC-4/AC-10 rather than re-running T-10 verbatim, or it fails against a criterion that no longer exists.",
    "The already-member claim path now redirects to the group page instead of showing an inline note; a claimant mid-race lands somewhere sensible, but it is a behavior change beyond the reported bug.",
    "End-to-end non-zero-balance blocking cannot exist until the expense/payment ledger does: the guard and message are enforced and unit-proven, but QA cannot drive a real non-zero balance on this ticket alone."
  ],
  "root_cause": "(1) Criterion defect behind T-10/BUG-2: the v1 AC-4 demanded an explicit naming confirm for rename, but docs/ui.md lists only delete-expense, delete-payment, remove-member, rotate/disable-invite and archive-group as confirm-gated, the suite's own passing T-5 drives rename as direct save plus success note, and RenameGroupForm has no ConfirmStep by design — the code was right and the criterion contradicted its own rule source, so no code change on rename can green the loop. (2) Code defect behind BUG-1: claim-failure feedback is stored as per-seat useActionState inside the ClaimSeatForm, while the action's blanket revalidatePath('/') refreshes the join page to zero seats and unmounts that exact form — the SEAT_TAKEN message the code sets is discarded with the component holding it, so the stale claimant sees a silent refresh. The v1 diagnosis proved state correctness (atomic UPDATE, 23505 mapping) but never message survivability.",
  "tests": [
    {
      "action": "edit",
      "cases": [
        "second sequential claim of the same seat redirects to /join/<token>?claim=taken instead of returning inline state (repro of BUG-1: the rejection must survive as a navigable message, not per-form state)",
        "claim by somebody who is already a member redirects to the group page",
        "claim against a seat in another group redirects to ?claim=taken",
        "failed claim writes no membership row and no duplicate member row; first-claim success redirect and ActivityEvent coverage unchanged"
      ],
      "path": "lib/groups/actions.test.ts"
    }
  ],
  "understanding": "The v1 work order was wrong about AC-4 and silent about the real BUG-1 mechanism. First, v1's AC-4 required an explicit naming confirm for rename alongside remove/archive/leave — but docs/ui.md gates only delete-expense, delete-payment, remove-member, rotate/disable-invite and archive-group behind confirms, the QA suite's own passing T-5 drives rename as fill plus Save name plus success note with no confirm step, and RenameGroupForm has no ConfirmStep by design. T-10 (fail) and T-5 (pass) cannot both be satisfied: adding a rename confirm to fix T-10 breaks T-5's save-then-note flow. So BUG-2/T-10 fails against the criterion's letter, not the code — the code was right, and AC-4 is amended here to exclude rename (kept at id AC-4, same position, per the root-cause agent's criterion-is-wrong rule) with the corrected expectation locked in as new AC-10. Second, BUG-1 is a genuine defect v1 never diagnosed: the losing double-claim IS rejected server-side (atomic UPDATE ... WHERE user_id IS NULL, correct), but the SEAT_TAKEN message is set on the per-seat ClaimSeatForm's useActionState while the action's blanket revalidatePath('/') refreshes the join page to zero seats, unmounting that very form — the intended rejection is never visible. The fix is therefore a different mechanism, not a re-roll: redirect-with-message (seat-taken to /join/<token>?claim=taken rendered at panel level, already-member to the group page) instead of in-place form state, covered by new AC-9.",
  "version": 2
}
